  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1033 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nUpper level ridging is expected to build in over the Panhandles \nWed into Thu raising daytime highs into the upper 70s to lower \n80s. The next upper level trough is progged to approach the \ncombined Panhandles Thu, raising surface winds a bit compared to \nthe calm winds expected Wed. This system may have the potential to\nbring the return of precipitation chances Thu night for the far \nwestern Panhandles. With the rest of the Panhandles gaining precip\nchances on Friday. There is a bit of uncertainty with the timing \nand coverage of potential showers/storms at this time. \nDeterministic models do not agree on the path and timing of the \nbest precipitation. Likely to see the rain chances to return, \nhowever, the details in amounts and coverage are not great at this\ntime. The current signals indicate a slight cool down Friday as \nwell with this system. Temperatures are expected to be in the \nlower to mid 70s in the western Panhandles and mid to upper 70s in\nthe eastern Panhandles Friday afternoon. Going into the weekend \nthe NBM is giving upper 60s to lower 70s for afternoon highs. &&",
